	(text "EoS STM32 64, rev A. Designed by Kartikeydheer Srivastava.\nCopyright (c) 2026 Kartikeydheer Srivastava. All rights reserved; see LICENSE.txt.\nValues from ST DS10314 Rev 8, RM0383 Rev 3, AN4488 Rev 7, AN2867 Rev 24, AN2606 Rev 70;\nSilicon Labs CP2102N Rev. 1.5; Diodes DS37274, DS41326, DS13004; Nexperia PMEG3010CEH;\nLittelfuse SP05xxBA; Bourns SRP5030T; ECS ECX-53B; Abracon ABS07-120; TDK MMZ1608; Kingbright.\nFirmware: HSE 8 MHz crystal (not bypass); LSE high drive (LSEMOD = 1);\nUSB: J2's VBUS on PC9 (JP7): keep the D+ pull-up off (SDIS) while PC9 is low.\nBOOT0: hold B3, press B2 (DFU). RDP Level 2 locks out SWD and DFU for good.\nIDD: cut JP1, ammeter across J4. JP8/JP9 cut: D0/D1 free of the COM port."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 330 380 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "60b5e0cb-952b-505e-8af8-0f4191a2cd5c")
	)
